turnip (guamp A610): tile memory (GMEM) again for multisampled passes under TU_DEBUG "sysmem" (TU_GUAMP_GMEM=none|msaa|owned|all, default msaa), exact tile stores where the aligned 16x4 blocks would leave a host-imported image, and pass counters for the plugin's rows (tu_guamp_render_counts)

The board's NativeTurnipDebug "nocb,noconform,sysmem" sends every pass to system memory. On the A610 (one CCU, 8 KiB of colour cache
in that mode) a multisampled pass writes and reads each sample in DRAM and resolves there again: Maps (VectorKit, 4x MSAA) at a few
fps, W5 gpu 50-80 ms a frame in fin50. TU_GUAMP_GMEM (one word: guamp-m2v-env=TU_GUAMP_GMEM=<word> sets it in every Metal process)
lets such passes go on to Turnip's own choice: none = as before, msaa = multisampled passes (default), owned = those and the passes
whose attachments are all Turnip's own memory (no IOSurface), all = "sysmem" ignored (the fin46d test, glitches).
The fast tile store writes whole gmem_align_w x gmem_align_h blocks past an unaligned edge "into padding space", which an image over a
host import (the caller's pitch and size) may not have: such a store now takes Turnip's exact (3D) path instead of writing into the
next row or past the memory, a probable cause of the fin46d GMEM glitches. Applies after the UniXNU Mesa patches and 0001-0002.

